    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483">

                <pb facs="0586" n="518" xml:id="pg518"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.857 L 97/126½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to President Wilson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 11, 1916</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: I have your comment upon
                    the proposed reply of the German Government in the Lusitania case. With your
                    views I entirely agree.</p>
                <p>Yesterday I had an interview with Count von Bernstorff, of which I enclose a
                    memorandum which was made immediately after I talked with him.<anchor n="97"
                        xml:id="d483-f1"/> You will perceive that I took very much the line of
                    approach which you suggest in your letter.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
